Package: mica-systemd
Version: 257.13-mica2
Source-Date-Epoch: 1790847060
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: mica-system, systemd, systemd-sysv, systemd-resolved, systemd-repart, systemd-timesyncd, udev
Provides: mica-init-system
Conflicts: mica-openrc
Description: Mica OS on systemd
 The init half of a Mica OS root that runs systemd, one of the two a product
 chooses (the other is mica-openrc): the units that run mica-system's tools --
 the DATA layout, the bind mounts of /mica, /mica/containers, /srv, /home,
 /root, /var, /var/lib/mica, /etc/hostname and /usr/local/lib/systemd/system,
 the seed and reconcile services, the health gate and the boot-failure handler,
 the offline provisioning import -- with the default DHCP network, volatile
 journald storage, the network time policy, the hardware watchdog and the drop
 of CAP_SYS_RESOURCE that keeps services inside DATA's project quotas;
 /usr/lib/mica/mica-init for systemd; and mica-grow-data, which grows DATA with
 systemd-repart.
 .
 Enablement is payload: the wants-links and /dev/null masks this package ships
 are the whole of it, and no maintainer script enables a unit. The preset
 50-mica-nftables.preset keeps nftables.service disabled wherever a product
 adds the firewall; the postinst refuses a root in which it is linked.
 .
 getty@.service and serial-getty@.service start only once the console option
 has installed /usr/bin/login. The console policy of every board: getty@tty1 is
 masked, so the VT the boot logo lands on stays idle even for logind's
 on-demand autovt, and logind reserves tty2 as the one login VT (NAutoVTs=0,
 ReserveVT=2).
